{"step_index":1061,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:24:54Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:24:54+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:25:00+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:24:54+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:25:00+08:00\nThe search for \"can javascript web app detect screenshot printscreen android ios browser limitations\" returned the following summary:\n**No, a standard JavaScript web application running inside a mobile browser (Android or iOS) cannot directly detect or prevent a user from taking a screenshot[1][2].** \n\nThe limitations preventing this stem from core web architecture, browser sandboxing[3][2], and operating system (OS) design.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Why Web Apps Can’t Do It (The Technical Limitations)\n\n* **The Sandbox Architecture:** Web browsers operate inside a strict security sandbox[3][2]. JavaScript code is restricted to what happens inside the specific browser tab. It has no visibility into system-level events[3][4].\n* **OS-Level Handling:** Taking a screenshot on Android (e.g., Power + Volume Down) or iOS (e.g., Side Button + Volume Up) is managed entirely by the mobile operating system[5][6][2]. The OS grabs the frame buffer directly from the hardware/graphics layer. It does not ping the browser, and the browser has no hook or API listening for that hardware interruption[7].\n* **No Standard Web API:** There is no W3C standard or browser API (like `navigator.onScreenshot`) available to web developers. \n\n---\n\n### 2. Platform-Specific Nuances (Android vs. iOS)\n\n#### **Android Mobile Browsers (Chrome, Firefox, Samsung Internet, etc.)**\n* **Detection:** Impossible via standard web code[1]. Even though Android 14 introduced a native *App* API for screenshot detection (`ScreenCaptureCallback`)[5][8], **this API is only exposed to native Android applications**, not to web browsers or websites running inside a browser tab.\n* **Prevention:** Native Android apps can use `FLAG_SECURE` to block screenshots entirely[9], but web browsers do not expose this flag to websites. \n\n#### **iOS Mobile Browsers (Safari, Chrome for iOS, etc.)**\n* **Detection:** Apple provides native API\n<truncated 3571 bytes>\nAqjmn5lpqQpaBUVugqw)\n[5] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFhGx-cdHAMGyJjmh9GZBHM8BYVr0KZno9Y5Saby3i4VM-0r6S6wv0uxcLBWt0LOG44cSLZziTsy1IaNpTX3P4dZl40TDx1IV9oazSmvvk2WuGG1haiWqZKY6R1EbnT689VF9VcTwHVII8CPl50U6qO5BZ7sVt_Qg9EG9mFRcI4w3YjdYZefshE2YLVlaE11t3PdkxNGsfMpD33YAjjarpo3xx-U85A0g==)\n[6] [ptkd.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHr2FxalnbhKsmYSeIFAyZ9NALG1Rha5_kneSgoKKOlgmp9Df3vqYSNsLN0QgaoonN9Y4l-l_yR2PLGtxfoVXFyFnHSxkjTazOuJ7Ci_YJj6U4hyESGC82BJvVBHWiLx0dV5SjGOjb-4Jx-je0QTYhJBlGBsJVx)\n[7] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFa-39YvE3pcHndOF-znZU8XgWn7hd2fGlCxddpnt2d77ODQApjNXrIcyCeEDstC9OoKDpcWN7fPA0hxEzko2U32l2foR5iJsn3y8jRDjBq3_a5MJyKnh8sN8GL4XterMkrWRIvrga3ZFAGPQaW7dSLhOCwvGJh3DyB3EGyIzU6z9tErVwdYW0Disk=)\n[8] [android.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFrVJ_4qKYrFzrL5uU0MWHhyAeOkUl62adW3e0N4q2znlHdwgQNSIPG2_E2om6bjOgorJhw64pnuqSNUvreT2zxkFunSavU1eCqfhFUz9GuzGp6o-BH3sNLKyX5IsRy7AbqsxaRrCvtFeyrC3tzVAEwhna58uHguesJZMNPCT8ydAMuWQ==)\n[9] [peakiq.in](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQG0_8S10C3TRqUE0zP_WpPhwAzXko7h7nf6UFTiYTIj2HCO_CdrDDnPFJ12wMspvMOmdTweDucYfBMIU2aTzPBJM3ChIQexnxCAtzkywZawRiFkBn7RjRth4SDxWDj_58HrZpGKEXCS3URPm7V9Z3rdUA415APU8ABwDWU=)\n[10] [alyamanalhayekdesign.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE62PXJmQKdnTIhybcjLJqBLokMscJ50wTTeV639w0srJWIk495-pN4tk3Oi33lTWpNOOK2wDZXG8DSX5pU5zM_keN6bICtYGFJ5YrvI8Tq4-A0Thw9LRo6WGLashnMyfcy2h6xtJ6IAH2ax1aZ8ctFRHVioxsEhjbmKRaN6_5iUbc=)\n[11] [reddit.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_owvP5RfKvZIk-wAzyzYiU4hJcFWRDOdcNpPfudKG2nxGhExwnQC7po0F3_d5xtlKK9FHFb4gMqZO09vLcdkNctywfr8OUWKA0dXWPUyhhDYQFY-zDk3n5KHGIsTBDDECZQJ_sgGKaTWOT6gN9KNaDO7Tf16jIW1h-LNJKyHUKyYnJ9T8h5SMPc6n4jsPR0FOSsS6M5vt6LRNvCRt)\n\nNote: Source URLs are HTTP redirects; check where they resolve if you need the direct link.","truncated_fields":["content"]}
{"step_index":1062,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-10T21:24:55Z","content":"Created At: 2026-11-11T05:24:55+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:25:04+08:00\nCreated At: 2026-11-11T05:24:55+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-11-11T05:25:04+08:00\nThe search for \"web browser detect mobile screenshot ios safari android chrome visibilitychange blur\" returned the following summary:\n**No, a web browser (like iOS Safari or Android Chrome) cannot directly detect when a user takes a native device screenshot[1].** \n\nUnlike native mobile apps (which have access to native SDK hooks or system flags like Android's `FLAG_SECURE`), web pages run inside a strict browser sandbox[1][2]. The operating system handles hardware button shortcuts (like Volume Down + Power) entirely outside the webpage's awareness[3].\n\nHowever, developers often look at events like `visibilitychange`, `blur`, or `focus` to manage application state when a user leaves the page. Here is how those events relate to mobile workflows and why they **cannot** reliably detect screenshots.\n\n---\n\n### Why `visibilitychange` and `blur` Do Not Detect Screenshots\n\n1. **iOS Safari:** \n   * When a user presses the hardware buttons to take a screenshot on an iPhone, **it does not trigger** `visibilitychange` or `blur`. The browser stays active in the foreground while the OS overlay flashes on top. \n   * The *only* time `visibilitychange` (state changing to `hidden`) or `blur` fires on iOS is when the user actually leaves Safari—such as swiping up to go to the home screen, switching apps, or pulling down the iOS Control Center (which triggers a blur/hide depending on iOS version).\n2. **Android Chrome:**\n   * Taking a standard screenshot via hardware keys **does not** trigger a page visibility or blur event. \n   * Newer versions of Android (Android 14+) introduced a system-level *Screenshot Detection API* for native apps[4], but **this API is not exposed to web browsers or JavaScript**.\n\n---\n\n### Code Example: What `visibilitychange` *Actually* Catches\nIf you implement standard visibility tracking, it will tell you when the user minimizes the browser or switches \n<truncated 1288 bytes>\ng on a mobile web browser[2][7].\n\nSources:\n[1] [aivideodetector.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFGXM7KJRybpflMiVw0l8FcDSZ7DhobJ-ndl6saxI4qOXTlb1zGqo5QMk9Ri6H4xFTsrbXcooTA19F7USxRWjhiHjm0Xxm3blVPO_wpu8FozHMc5VeXIPcltkVePQ2zhLBhDbdtDmw7xBDdKm7DF2ZidiYsjHZpwQ6cpUb8mzQ=)\n[2] [peakiq.in](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQF0vs_zm9e4W83jlnmivu34aGymNnUsjcNuqgzRrUBdTuKabardbselp6ys6aqcskjnLMlKFmQ08pkwZmoHHLGfnpHPGBtksHj5eAOqzEOUzWR0SziTXSxvoKoll6ya-qkJtsEW0uWae64BSZY2PXe81861z969HrwLuA==)\n[3] [aivideodetector.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFGXM7KJRybpflMiVw0l8FcDSZ7DhobJ-ndl6saxI4qOXTlb1zGqo5QMk9Ri6H4xFTsrbXcooTA19F7USxRWjhiHjm0Xxm3blVPO_wpu8FozHMc5VeXIPcltkVePQ2zhLBhDbdtDmw7xBDdKm7DF2ZidiYsjHZpwQ6cpUb8mzQ=)\n[4] [android.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEEu0ZI8K1nmHz0loOLp1fe3j57G5h7Z7bVsa5wNvOtHs7orW0_zz210a4nzK2_xoPYXwjcWKhhA3c0Nqs_m2pryZ0Ulk1EcSzQBvJj8aZ8J4vE-xOwYQEgVTQFb0o4aocpYwuFLAkjAxB-FxEzSzYo-GQg1SNBAXGaxJq0VWCikLGk)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGHznk93fzqNQwdIl12zq4eTH6KUzaHxKOrCBTgX-gCXQecyj7xtSeOcjGpQ7NHhhTTKwPbQQIETTIMw_jxqeWdKX6sc45rUPPj4bB6Qu0CykQgbHzJz7cbcNT9V_ov9JHlYnU-Qpt6CNg0tIUM_WBXC0C6Uz0nLPdDSSwYSy5sNKKs0BQ1-h1DkGX_Ik3PSY19Ce5WS8h5KFZT-jef7gbXvSIWE8ff6qNeUA==)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGrHKD9onFWBzaqrkw8Y9Kedz5jxXHA8i9zCDcITtxyvQ3MuwHnPVdjVf102duMw83YAwm7n-ubgNqv9r3eWlgBktBzdsNNQH-hbmLxTxSBDB-3Nrqa5NEX4uVaNAxDMuTr02Iur6r98q7Swneu-CaGaD_HbJFpUJP7h3YDd0_zqZODmNxcYrWQbw==)\n[7] [proandroiddev.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api